      "summaries": {
        "en": "MOSS-TTS is an open-source family of speech and sound generation models designed for high-fidelity, expressive audio in complex real-world scenarios. Its key technical insight is a unified architecture combining audio tokenization with large language models, enabling tasks like long-form speech, multi-speaker dialogue, voice cloning, and environmental sound effects. You can use it via Python for streaming TTS, custom voice design, or integrating into multimodal applications, making advanced audio generation accessible.",
        "zh": "MOSS-TTS 是一个开源语音与音效生成模型家族，旨在解决复杂真实场景下的高保真、高表现力音频生成问题。其核心技术亮点是将音频分词器与大语言模型统一架构，从而支持长文本语音、多说话人对话、声音克隆、环境音效以及实时流式TTS等多种任务。你可以通过Python接口直接使用，进行自定义声音设计、流式语音合成，或将其集成到多模态应用中。这一设计让开发者无需深厚音频专业知识，即可构建富有表现力的语音交互系统。",
        "es": "MOSS-TTS is an open-source family of speech and sound generation models designed for high-fidelity, expressive audio in complex real-world scenarios. Its key technical insight is a unified architecture combining audio tokenization with large language models, enabling tasks like long-form speech, multi-speaker dialogue, voice cloning, and environmental sound effects. You can use it via Python for streaming TTS, custom voice design, or integrating into multimodal applications, making advanced audio generation accessible.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "MOSS-TTS stands out for audio, audio-tokenizer, and llm in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "MOSS-TTS is an open-source family of speech and sound generation models designed for high-fidelity, expressive audio in complex real-world scenarios. Its key technical insight is a unified architecture combining audio tokenization with large language models, enabling tasks like long-form speech, multi-speaker dialogue, voice cloning, and environmental sound effects. You can use it via Python for streaming TTS, custom voice design, or integrating into multimodal applications, making advanced audio generation accessible.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-TTS for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
